{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/LSTM Forget Gate.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/LSTM Forget Gate.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"lstm forget gate lstm forget gate","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/LSTM Forget Gate.md","fileName":"LSTM Forget Gate.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"LSTM Forget Gate","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 02:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Recurrent Sequence Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Recurrent Sequence Architecture","LSTM Cell State","LSTM Input Gate","LSTM Output Gate","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/LSTM Forget Gate.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/LSTM Forget Gate.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"lstm forget gate lstm forget gate","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/LSTM Forget Gate.md","fileName":"LSTM Forget Gate.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"LSTM Forget Gate","heading":"LSTM Forget Gate","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An LSTM forget gate decides how much of the previous [[LSTM Cell State|cell state]] to retain at a new sequence step. It processes the current input together with the prior hidden output using sigmoid units, producing a vector of values between zero and one.\n\nMultiplying the old cell state elementwise by this vector suppresses entries with gate values near zero and retains entries with values near one. The gate's role is selective memory removal, distinct from adding new information through the [[LSTM Input Gate]] or deciding what to reveal through the [[LSTM Output Gate]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Recurrent Sequence Architecture","LSTM Cell State","LSTM Input Gate","LSTM Output Gate","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/LSTM Forget Gate.md::2","sourceKey":